                <pb facs="0233" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 18643/13.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Dudley.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Knox directs Ambassador Dudley to express the high appreciation of the
                    Government of the United States of the action of the Brazilian Congress in
                    extending and continuing the list of American products to enjoy preferential
                    tariff treatment.</p>
            </div>
